1
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:40,236
-Isn't that funny? -Oh, how weird.

2
00:01:46,843 --> 00:01:48,845
All right, it's done!

3
00:01:49,379 --> 00:01:52,015
Thank you for working on New Year's Day.

4
00:01:52,215 --> 00:01:54,250
We'll take over from here.

5
00:01:54,817 --> 00:01:56,419
Thanks guys.

6
00:01:56,619 --> 00:02:00,089
Ryo-san, I hear you've been working since New Year's Eve.

7
00:02:00,523 --> 00:02:01,758
Damn straight!

8
00:02:01,991 --> 00:02:06,863
Unlike Nakagawa and Reiko, I put my life on the line for the station.

9
00:02:07,063 --> 00:02:12,301
My passion to protect the people never dies out. Not even for New Year's.

10
00:02:12,535 --> 00:02:13,770
What's so funny!

11
00:02:14,003 --> 00:02:17,240
Ryo-san, please limit your jokes to your monobrow.

12
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:18,274
What?

13
00:02:18,474 --> 00:02:21,577
We know you took too much time off last summer,

14
00:02:21,778 --> 00:02:24,480
and now you have to make it up over New Year's.

15
00:02:25,047 --> 00:02:26,883
Nothing gets past you two.

16
00:02:29,485 --> 00:02:31,120
Well, I'd better get going.

17
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:32,955
Ryo-san, what's your plan now?

18
00:02:33,189 --> 00:02:35,491
Have some chilled sake, then hit the hay.

19
00:02:35,958 --> 00:02:38,594
Chief's not throwing a party this year.

20
00:02:38,795 --> 00:02:40,396
Oh? You sure?

21
00:02:40,596 --> 00:02:43,466
I saw Terai yesterday at the shrine.

22
00:02:43,666 --> 00:02:48,104
He said he was going to the chief's house in his new kimono to pay his respects.

23
00:02:48,471 --> 00:02:50,673
You must have heard wrong.

24
00:02:50,907 --> 00:02:55,144
The chief said he was going on a trip with just his family.

25
00:02:57,213 --> 00:02:58,114
A New Year's party?

26
00:02:58,514 --> 00:03:01,284
Yeah, the annual New Year's party at your house.

27
00:03:01,984 --> 00:03:03,920
When's it going to be?

28
00:03:04,487 --> 00:03:06,989
Um... We're not having one this time.

29
00:03:07,423 --> 00:03:09,759
What?

30
00:03:11,494 --> 00:03:17,500
But the chief's New Year osechi food is my favorite part of the year...

31
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:20,303
Ryo-chan, you're always exaggerating.

32
00:03:21,904 --> 00:03:23,272
It's not that bad.

33
00:03:24,006 --> 00:03:27,343
I'm going on a hot spring trip with just the family.

34
00:03:28,077 --> 00:03:30,847
So you're putting your family before your employees?

35
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,448
Don't say that.

36
00:03:32,648 --> 00:03:34,083
Hiromi's not a kid anymore,

37
00:03:34,283 --> 00:03:38,354
so we don't often get the chance to go away as just the three of us.

38
00:03:38,855 --> 00:03:40,723
Anyway, that's how it is.

39
00:03:40,957 --> 00:03:43,526
You'll just have to wait until the following year.

40
00:03:43,860 --> 00:03:44,861
R-Right...

41
00:03:45,094 --> 00:03:47,797
I-It's a real shame...

42
00:03:49,332 --> 00:03:53,402
Now that I think about it, everyone was acting quite odd.

43
00:03:53,636 --> 00:03:56,372
Could it be that they intentionally left me out?

44
00:03:56,572 --> 00:03:57,306
That does it!

45
00:04:03,646 --> 00:04:06,516
Is this Terai-san's house? I'm Ryotsu.

46
00:04:06,716 --> 00:04:08,151
Happy New Year.

47
00:04:08,351 --> 00:04:11,854
Hey, I have something I need to ask Terai.

48
00:04:15,525 --> 00:04:16,425
What?!

49
00:04:19,962 --> 00:04:23,032
That no-good, lying chief!

50
00:04:23,232 --> 00:04:26,569
He left me out! Damn him!

51
00:04:27,336 --> 00:04:31,240
I'm gonna eat his New Year's food no matter what!

52
00:04:34,744 --> 00:04:36,979
I'm coming for you, Chief!

53
00:04:37,847 --> 00:04:40,983
Was that a chainsaw?

54
00:04:41,183 --> 00:04:43,052
Heads are gonna roll.

55
00:04:46,022 --> 00:04:48,357
Happy New Year!

56
00:04:48,558 --> 00:04:51,427
I look forward to working with you all again this year.

57
00:04:52,762 --> 00:04:55,097
Hiromi-chan, you look nice.

58
00:04:55,331 --> 00:04:57,233
And you look nice too, Reiko-san.

59
00:04:57,433 --> 00:04:58,434
Thank you.

60
00:04:58,801 --> 00:05:01,437
Hey, is Ryotsu not here yet?

61
00:05:02,939 --> 00:05:03,639
Huh?

62
00:05:06,342 --> 00:05:07,910
You know, Dad...

63
00:05:08,110 --> 00:05:12,748
Hiromi. I don't want to have to think about that guy during New Year's.

64
00:05:12,949 --> 00:05:15,818
Nakagawa. Did you park just outside?

65
00:05:16,219 --> 00:05:17,820
Y-Yes...

66
00:05:18,054 --> 00:05:21,357
Come, come. It's a bit cramped, but come on in.

67
00:05:21,924 --> 00:05:22,725
Huh?

68
00:05:23,192 --> 00:05:26,629
Why are your shutters closed during the day?

69
00:05:27,363 --> 00:05:29,765
Let's just say it's to prevent bad luck.

70
00:05:29,966 --> 00:05:31,901
Bad luck?

71
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:37,039
Ouch! Please, let go!

72
00:05:37,239 --> 00:05:40,509
I was about to do the New Year's shrine visit with my sister.

73
00:05:40,743 --> 00:05:45,281
You can go to the shrine any time. Chief's New Year's party is only today!

74
00:05:45,481 --> 00:05:47,283
There's no need to get extreme...

75
00:05:47,483 --> 00:05:48,684
Doesn't it bother you?

76
00:05:49,285 --> 00:05:51,787
You didn't get an invite either.

77
00:05:51,988 --> 00:05:52,989
Why would I?

78
00:05:53,222 --> 00:05:56,158
I'm a motorcycle cop. I don't work in the station.

79
00:05:56,392 --> 00:05:58,327
Stop splitting hairs.

80
00:05:58,527 --> 00:06:01,931
You're my good friend, so just take me to the chief's house!

81
00:06:21,017 --> 00:06:23,786
You really don't waste time in being a pushy dude.

82
00:06:24,787 --> 00:06:27,156
All right. Move your butt and let's go.

83
00:06:28,324 --> 00:06:29,258
Here we go!

84
00:06:42,505 --> 00:06:44,206
Oh, thank you.

85
00:06:45,708 --> 00:06:47,043
What's up, Nakagawa?

86
00:06:47,877 --> 00:06:51,514
Wasn't that the sound of Honda-san's CBX?

87
00:06:52,281 --> 00:06:54,183
Maybe Ryotsu's with him?

88
00:06:54,383 --> 00:06:55,351
What?

89
00:06:55,718 --> 00:06:57,520
How did he sniff us out already?

90
00:06:58,054 --> 00:07:00,556
I knew bad luck had a keen sense of smell.

91
00:07:01,223 --> 00:07:05,728
Listen up. No matter what happens, no one makes a sound or goes outside.

92
00:07:17,039 --> 00:07:20,042
Grr, he's pretending not to be home.

93
00:07:20,409 --> 00:07:23,179
You know, he really could be on a family trip?

94
00:07:23,379 --> 00:07:26,015
Not a chance. Look over there.

95
00:07:27,683 --> 00:07:28,851
What's that?

96
00:07:29,952 --> 00:07:32,855
Covering it with a sheet? What a cheap trick!

97
00:07:37,326 --> 00:07:39,228
It's a Ferrari F50!

98
00:07:39,428 --> 00:07:43,599
It's not the one he usually drives, but it's definitely one of Nakagawa's.

99
00:07:43,799 --> 00:07:48,037
Are you sure? It could belong to one of the neighbors.

100
00:07:48,237 --> 00:07:49,438
Look around you!

101
00:07:50,072 --> 00:07:52,108
Do you see any neighbors?

102
00:07:52,608 --> 00:07:55,177
-And look at the license plate. -Huh?

103
00:07:55,878 --> 00:07:57,513
It's a Shonan plate.

104
00:07:57,913 --> 00:08:00,249
Nakagawa lives in Tokyo,

105
00:08:00,449 --> 00:08:04,286
but he likes to show off by getting all his cars Shonan plates.

106
00:08:09,358 --> 00:08:10,893
Ohara-san!

107
00:08:11,594 --> 00:08:14,730
It's the mailman. I need a signature.

108
00:08:15,431 --> 00:08:18,000
Ohara-san! Please answer the door!

109
00:08:18,434 --> 00:08:20,536
Ryo-chan's so obvious.

110
00:08:21,137 --> 00:08:23,305
I can't bear this...

111
00:08:26,742 --> 00:08:29,845
Damn you... You're really going to pretend you're not home?

112
00:08:30,312 --> 00:08:33,382
All the windows are shuttered, and the curtains are drawn.

113
00:08:33,582 --> 00:08:35,951
They must be on holiday.

114
00:08:36,152 --> 00:08:39,021
-Oh! The enemy must be inside! -Huh?

115
00:08:39,255 --> 00:08:40,289
Look at this!

116
00:08:41,323 --> 00:08:44,093
It's just an electricity meter.

117
00:08:44,293 --> 00:08:46,128
Watch the meter carefully.

118
00:08:46,862 --> 00:08:50,232
If they were out, only the fridge and the phone would be left on.

119
00:08:50,433 --> 00:08:52,635
It wouldn't be ticking over this much.

120
00:08:52,835 --> 00:08:54,170
Well spotted.

121
00:08:54,703 --> 00:08:56,806
Would anyone like some sukiyaki?

122
00:08:57,006 --> 00:09:00,609
Sounds good! I was just thinking I've hit my New Year's osechi limit.

123
00:09:00,810 --> 00:09:02,178
I'll help serve.

124
00:09:02,411 --> 00:09:03,179
Chief!

125
00:09:03,412 --> 00:09:04,113
Hmm?

126
00:09:04,313 --> 00:09:05,848
I know you're in there!

127
00:09:06,449 --> 00:09:07,450
He just won't quit.

128
00:09:07,650 --> 00:09:10,453
Let us in right now!

129
00:09:10,653 --> 00:09:13,956
Dad, I feel bad for them. We should let them in.

130
00:09:14,156 --> 00:09:14,957
No!

131
00:09:15,291 --> 00:09:19,962
You may not know this, but that man ruins my house every single New Year's!

132
00:09:20,696 --> 00:09:24,033
He ruined my bonsai trees that time we played shuttlecock.

133
00:09:24,266 --> 00:09:26,502
He stained the tatami during calligraphy.

134
00:09:26,702 --> 00:09:29,471
And when I told him off, he smeared ink on my face!

135
00:09:29,672 --> 00:09:33,542
The whole room was covered in black by the time we were finished!

136
00:09:34,076 --> 00:09:36,712
That man is never entering my house again.

137
00:09:36,912 --> 00:09:41,450
It's understandable why he'd want to exclude Ryotsu...

138
00:09:41,650 --> 00:09:44,086
You're completely surrounded!

139
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:46,055
Give up and come out!

140
00:09:46,288 --> 00:09:47,056
Ignore him.

141
00:09:48,057 --> 00:09:50,459
There's no reaction at all.

142
00:09:50,659 --> 00:09:55,698
Damn it! If this is how he wants to play, I'll use my trump card to force my way in.

143
00:09:55,898 --> 00:09:57,032
Your trump card?

144
00:09:58,367 --> 00:10:00,102
He's quietened down now.

145
00:10:01,237 --> 00:10:03,038
Guess he's finally given up.

146
00:10:03,239 --> 00:10:04,006
I doubt it.

147
00:10:04,206 --> 00:10:08,077
Ryotsu is extraordinarily tenacious when it comes to food.

148
00:10:08,310 --> 00:10:09,845
We're not out of the woods yet.

149
00:10:10,746 --> 00:10:12,047
Did the power go out?

150
00:10:12,548 --> 00:10:15,351
They wouldn't do electrical work during New Year's.

151
00:10:15,551 --> 00:10:19,054
Honey, the kitchen gas has been cut too.

152
00:10:19,255 --> 00:10:20,189
What?

153
00:10:21,090 --> 00:10:24,093
Damn that Ryotsu. This is his doing!

154
00:10:24,593 --> 00:10:28,597
Ryotsu. I think that's enough.

155
00:10:28,797 --> 00:10:32,868
No way! I'm going to eat my New Year's osechi no matter what!

156
00:10:34,270 --> 00:10:36,205
They sure are stubborn.

157
00:10:36,405 --> 00:10:41,043
I'd like to make 'em squirm by reversing the water and the sewage,

158
00:10:41,243 --> 00:10:43,913
but let's speed things up and break down the door.

159
00:10:44,113 --> 00:10:45,381
W-Wait, Ryotsu!

160
00:10:50,519 --> 00:10:53,422
Ryotsu, brandishing a chainsaw is a bit too far...

161
00:10:53,822 --> 00:10:56,358
It's fine, Honda. Don't worry.

162
00:10:56,558 --> 00:10:57,159
Huh?

163
00:10:57,693 --> 00:10:59,628
I'll use only the lightest touch.

164
00:11:00,095 --> 00:11:02,131
That's not reassuring at all.

165
00:11:03,065 --> 00:11:04,767
Here I go!

166
00:11:06,368 --> 00:11:07,970
Damn it, Ryotsu!

167
00:11:19,081 --> 00:11:23,319
Chief! Don't open the door like that! You took years off my life!

168
00:11:23,552 --> 00:11:26,322
It's my life you almost shaved off there!

169
00:11:26,555 --> 00:11:30,159
What are you doing here with a chainsaw?

170
00:11:30,392 --> 00:11:36,165
The door... Uh, I mean... the chief asked me to take care of his plants.

171
00:11:36,598 --> 00:11:39,935
You're lying! I don't remember asking you to do that.

172
00:11:40,135 --> 00:11:43,639
Oh dear. You must be getting forgetful in your old age.

173
00:11:43,839 --> 00:11:44,974
Right, Honda?

174
00:11:45,174 --> 00:11:46,675
Right. No, I mean...

175
00:11:47,743 --> 00:11:51,413
But hey, weren't you meant to be on a hot spring trip with the family?

176
00:11:52,614 --> 00:11:56,518
Well, there was... a mistake by the travel agency.

177
00:11:56,752 --> 00:11:59,421
We couldn't get tickets, so we just stayed home.

178
00:12:00,222 --> 00:12:02,591
Then why is Nakagawa here?

179
00:12:04,226 --> 00:12:09,064
Well, since I had some free time, I invited Nakagawa and the others.

180
00:12:09,798 --> 00:12:14,703
Obviously I tried to contact you at home, but unfortunately you weren't there.

181
00:12:14,903 --> 00:12:19,208
Of course I wasn't! I was working at the station the whole time.

182
00:12:19,441 --> 00:12:21,243
Oh, you were...?

183
00:12:22,311 --> 00:12:23,879
How could I forget?

184
00:12:25,381 --> 00:12:29,818
Well, lady luck smiles upon us now. Shall we drop in, Honda?

185
00:12:30,919 --> 00:12:33,222
I assume you don't mind, Chief?

186
00:12:33,689 --> 00:12:34,923
Not at all...

187
00:12:35,391 --> 00:12:38,827
Good thing, right Honda? After coming all this way for plants.

188
00:12:39,028 --> 00:12:39,828
Uh, yeah...

189
00:12:40,029 --> 00:12:42,731
All right then. Let's have some osechi food!

190
00:12:42,931 --> 00:12:44,166
Oh! Before that...

191
00:12:50,239 --> 00:12:51,407
Now I'm ready.

192
00:12:51,907 --> 00:12:55,077
Hm? You're quite well prepared for someone who came to garden.

193
00:12:55,277 --> 00:12:58,580
I brought it so I wouldn't be caught out in this situation.

194
00:12:58,814 --> 00:13:01,383
Honda, it's a bit rude to be wearing that outfit.

195
00:13:01,583 --> 00:13:04,386
Oh well, it's only the chief's house.

196
00:13:05,921 --> 00:13:10,392
Ryotsu, I'll get you for this!

197
00:13:22,838 --> 00:13:25,941
Ryotsu-san, Honda-san, Happy New Year.

198
00:13:26,375 --> 00:13:27,609
Come, sit down.

199
00:13:27,843 --> 00:13:28,944
Thanks.

200
00:13:29,445 --> 00:13:32,381
Well, Happy New Year to all those who got an invite.

201
00:13:32,581 --> 00:13:34,750
Happy New Year...

202
00:13:34,950 --> 00:13:38,754
Terai, your new kimono looks great on you.

203
00:13:39,121 --> 00:13:40,856
How did you know it was new?

204
00:13:41,056 --> 00:13:43,859
A New Year's party worthy of such a nice new kimono...

205
00:13:44,059 --> 00:13:47,796
Don't you think you could have at least mentioned it to me?

206
00:13:49,231 --> 00:13:53,135
We're really lucky to have such great colleagues. Right, Honda?

207
00:13:53,335 --> 00:13:54,470
Ryotsu...

208
00:13:54,703 --> 00:13:58,807
Ryo-chan! Stop complaining through sarcasm.

209
00:13:59,007 --> 00:13:59,942
What did you say?

210
00:14:00,142 --> 00:14:03,312
Come on, it's New Year's. Let's all get along.

211
00:14:04,146 --> 00:14:08,150
We're done with the New Year's food, so we were thinking of having sukiyaki.

212
00:14:08,350 --> 00:14:09,818
Would you two like some?

213
00:14:10,986 --> 00:14:13,555
What a disgraceful thing to do!

214
00:14:13,756 --> 00:14:18,727
New Year's is for eating osechi. Isn't that just common sense, Chief?

215
00:14:18,927 --> 00:14:20,295
Yes, but...

216
00:14:20,929 --> 00:14:23,632
Osechi on New Year's isn't just for show.

217
00:14:23,832 --> 00:14:26,268
Osechi food keeps for a long time,

218
00:14:26,468 --> 00:14:29,638
so we eat it over New Year's to give the wife a break.

219
00:14:30,105 --> 00:14:33,842
It's time-honored wisdom direct from Japan!

220
00:14:34,943 --> 00:14:38,180
It's not like Ryo-chan has any right to be bossy about it.

221
00:14:39,815 --> 00:14:41,683
And each dish means something.

222
00:14:42,184 --> 00:14:45,788
The konbu-maki represents joy. The black beans are for working hard.

223
00:14:45,988 --> 00:14:49,124
The shrimp bring good fortune, and so on, so forth.

224
00:14:49,625 --> 00:14:53,395
What are you thinking serving sukiyaki on New Year's Day?

225
00:14:53,629 --> 00:14:56,365
Osechi is what you eat for New Year's in Japan!

226
00:14:56,598 --> 00:15:00,869
It looks like he came for the osechi, so you should serve it to him.

227
00:15:01,770 --> 00:15:03,038
So it seems.

228
00:15:03,605 --> 00:15:07,209
There's still some osechi left, right? Could you bring it out?

229
00:15:07,409 --> 00:15:08,043
Okay.

230
00:15:09,178 --> 00:15:11,647
All right! Here comes the osechi!

231
00:15:11,847 --> 00:15:16,418
We're going to have sukiyaki here, so you can eat the osechi over there.

232
00:15:20,889 --> 00:15:22,791
Tch, excluded again?

233
00:15:23,392 --> 00:15:25,661
Well, whatever. As long as I have my osechi.

234
00:15:25,861 --> 00:15:27,062
Here it comes!

235
00:15:27,262 --> 00:15:28,397
Here you are.

236
00:15:28,630 --> 00:15:30,332
Thanks!

237
00:15:30,532 --> 00:15:31,700
What?

238
00:15:34,236 --> 00:15:38,841
Uh, excuse me? I can't seem to see any kinton or kazunoko...

239
00:15:39,041 --> 00:15:42,211
We ate it all. What you've got there is all that's left.

240
00:15:42,411 --> 00:15:47,015
Oh? Black beans, konbu-maki, kamaboko...

241
00:15:47,216 --> 00:15:51,286
So all that's left are the three least popular osechi dishes...

242
00:15:55,591 --> 00:16:00,195
Osechi without the main dishes is not going to be any good at all.

243
00:16:01,430 --> 00:16:02,898
It looks delicious!

244
00:16:03,232 --> 00:16:05,934
All right, it's almost ready to eat.

245
00:16:06,134 --> 00:16:07,402
Um, Chief...

246
00:16:08,036 --> 00:16:09,204
Shall we eat?

247
00:16:09,404 --> 00:16:10,439
Yes, please!

248
00:16:10,672 --> 00:16:12,107
Um, Chief...

249
00:16:12,941 --> 00:16:13,742
What is it?

250
00:16:13,942 --> 00:16:16,945
If you like, I can help you with the sukiyaki over there.

251
00:16:17,145 --> 00:16:20,249
We served that osechi just for you!

252
00:16:20,449 --> 00:16:23,785
You can't have sukiyaki until you've finished your osechi!

253
00:16:24,253 --> 00:16:28,223
Fine, fine. As long as I finish it, right?

254
00:16:28,690 --> 00:16:29,858
Of course.

255
00:16:30,058 --> 00:16:34,329
This is perfect. I was worried about what to do with the leftovers.

256
00:16:34,563 --> 00:16:36,131
He's like a garbage disposal.

257
00:16:36,632 --> 00:16:39,501
Ryo-chan's got a stomach made of steel.

258
00:16:39,735 --> 00:16:43,071
Exactly. Even if the food is off, his stomach can handle it.

259
00:16:44,806 --> 00:16:49,344
But we'd better eat this meat before Ryotsu finishes the osechi.

260
00:16:49,578 --> 00:16:50,412
Okay.

261
00:16:55,751 --> 00:16:58,153
Now it's finally time for some sukiyaki.

262
00:16:58,353 --> 00:17:00,188
I'll just scooch in and... Huh?

263
00:17:02,424 --> 00:17:04,993
There's only one piece of meat!

264
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:06,795
Curse you!

265
00:17:08,330 --> 00:17:09,164
What?

266
00:17:10,165 --> 00:17:11,833
Sorry, Ryotsu.

267
00:17:12,067 --> 00:17:14,002
I was faster.

268
00:17:14,369 --> 00:17:16,271
No, I got it first!

269
00:17:16,471 --> 00:17:17,506
Right, Honda?

270
00:17:17,739 --> 00:17:19,374
Tell him, Honda.

271
00:17:20,809 --> 00:17:22,544
I think it's a tie...

272
00:17:22,778 --> 00:17:25,914
The elderly should cut back on their meat intake!

273
00:17:26,114 --> 00:17:29,685
You're the one who should refrain, seeing as you ate so much osechi!

274
00:17:33,188 --> 00:17:35,090
You leave me no choice...

275
00:17:36,291 --> 00:17:39,294
You can try to spit on it, but I won't let you.

276
00:17:39,494 --> 00:17:42,197
I see through your dirty tricks.

277
00:17:42,397 --> 00:17:43,365
Damn it!

278
00:17:44,032 --> 00:17:46,301
Look, you two. You're acting like children.

279
00:17:46,501 --> 00:17:49,805
Hey, why not decide who gets to eat it by having a competition?

280
00:17:50,339 --> 00:17:51,540
A competition?

281
00:17:51,773 --> 00:17:55,310
It's New Year's, so how about Karuta?

282
00:17:55,510 --> 00:17:57,379
That sounds like fun.

283
00:17:58,213 --> 00:17:59,047
Fine by me.

284
00:17:59,247 --> 00:18:01,383
We might have some Police Karuta around.

285
00:18:01,817 --> 00:18:03,719
Police Karuta?

286
00:18:03,952 --> 00:18:06,188
I played that with my sister yesterday.

287
00:18:06,388 --> 00:18:08,557
"A rolling detective gathers cases."

288
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:11,393
Or "A patrol in time saves nine."

289
00:18:11,593 --> 00:18:13,161
It's clever, isn't it?

290
00:18:13,595 --> 00:18:17,399
Traffic safety slogan Karuta is no fun.

291
00:18:17,599 --> 00:18:20,202
How about we play my version of Karuta?

292
00:18:20,402 --> 00:18:22,204
You brought a game of Karuta?

293
00:18:22,404 --> 00:18:27,175
Yeah. I made it at work over New Year's, just in case something like this happened.

294
00:18:28,243 --> 00:18:29,511
But you were on duty!

295
00:18:30,011 --> 00:18:33,181
Are we gonna play Kameari Park Police Station Karuta or not?

296
00:18:33,382 --> 00:18:37,419
Let's play. I'm going to win for sure, and you're not going to get any meat.

297
00:18:37,619 --> 00:18:40,222
No way! I'm gonna get that meat for sure!

298
00:18:42,391 --> 00:18:43,625
It'll be cold anyway.

299
00:18:46,561 --> 00:18:48,530
Okay, I'll start.

300
00:18:50,766 --> 00:18:52,634
What's the matter? Just read it.

301
00:18:53,935 --> 00:18:55,604
I can't read this out loud.

302
00:18:55,837 --> 00:18:58,106
-Nakagawa-san, you take over! -Eh?

303
00:18:58,306 --> 00:19:00,275
Somebody read it already!

304
00:19:00,709 --> 00:19:02,310
Okay, I will.

305
00:19:03,445 --> 00:19:05,714
"Time conquers all, like Reiko's knockers."

306
00:19:06,047 --> 00:19:07,649
What?!

307
00:19:07,883 --> 00:19:09,751
No, I was just...

308
00:19:09,951 --> 00:19:10,652
Mine!

309
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:15,657
One point to me, Chief. I found the matching card.

310
00:19:18,427 --> 00:19:20,062
What sort of filth is that?

311
00:19:20,395 --> 00:19:21,396
So uncouth...

312
00:19:21,596 --> 00:19:23,865
Okay, next one.

313
00:19:24,065 --> 00:19:27,202
"Not if, but when. Kankichi Ryotsu becomes Chief."

314
00:19:27,402 --> 00:19:28,870
What?!

315
00:19:29,571 --> 00:19:30,672
Got it!

316
00:19:32,074 --> 00:19:34,142
This is my favorite card.

317
00:19:34,342 --> 00:19:37,579
Ryotsu made these cards. Of course they're crazy.

318
00:19:39,047 --> 00:19:42,317
"Darkness is cheap, and Chief Ohara likes it."

319
00:19:42,517 --> 00:19:43,885
What?!

320
00:19:44,085 --> 00:19:44,820
There!

321
00:19:46,154 --> 00:19:48,323
Too bad. It was right in front of you.

322
00:19:51,126 --> 00:19:54,296
"Terai-kun. Slave to the lender."

323
00:19:54,496 --> 00:19:56,598
Let's see...

324
00:19:58,667 --> 00:19:59,534
There it is!

325
00:20:00,135 --> 00:20:01,837
Too slow, Chief!

326
00:20:02,070 --> 00:20:05,941
It seems you're no match for a Karuta master like me.

327
00:20:07,476 --> 00:20:09,311
These cards are bogus!

328
00:20:09,511 --> 00:20:12,514
You made them yourself, so you have an advantage!

329
00:20:12,714 --> 00:20:15,617
Are you complaining just because you're losing?

330
00:20:15,817 --> 00:20:19,387
I am not complaining. Your writing is just too messy to read.

331
00:20:19,621 --> 00:20:22,023
It's not fair that only you can read them.

332
00:20:24,493 --> 00:20:28,296
Hey, Chief. Where are you going with the picture cards?

333
00:20:29,364 --> 00:20:31,967
I'm making it fair by scattering them around.

334
00:20:35,036 --> 00:20:37,138
Are you going all around the house?

335
00:20:37,672 --> 00:20:39,641
This will be much fairer.

336
00:20:44,145 --> 00:20:45,280
Okay, now we're good.

337
00:20:45,947 --> 00:20:48,750
Nakagawa will read, and we'll find the pictures.

338
00:20:49,284 --> 00:20:52,354
Bring it back to Nakagawa for him to check if it's correct.

339
00:20:52,554 --> 00:20:54,022
Sounds like fun.

340
00:20:54,222 --> 00:20:55,490
Right, let's go!

341
00:20:55,690 --> 00:20:56,758
O-Okay...

342
00:20:57,559 --> 00:21:00,228
"Nakagawa-kun, dips his toes into policework."

343
00:21:00,695 --> 00:21:01,897
-"Nakagawa?" -Let's go!

344
00:21:05,133 --> 00:21:07,235
Yes! I've got it!

345
00:21:07,569 --> 00:21:09,237
Damn you!

346
00:21:09,437 --> 00:21:13,241
"To be the best, you have to be Kankichi Ryotsu."

347
00:21:13,975 --> 00:21:17,212
"Honda-kun has loved and lost more times than a man can count."

348
00:21:18,446 --> 00:21:21,750
"Fortune and Pachinko favor Ryo-san!"

349
00:21:22,517 --> 00:21:26,321
"Raise our pay, not our blood pressure, Chief."

350
00:21:28,690 --> 00:21:31,426
Ryo-chan has 20 cards, and the chief has 19.

351
00:21:31,626 --> 00:21:33,528
There are only two cards left.

352
00:21:35,163 --> 00:21:37,532
I can't lose to Ryotsu!

353
00:21:40,168 --> 00:21:44,172
I know one card is in the bathroom, and the other is in the study upstairs.

354
00:21:44,372 --> 00:21:47,576
"Terai's wife's box lunches are like pearls before swine!"

355
00:21:47,776 --> 00:21:48,910
The bathroom!

356
00:21:49,277 --> 00:21:49,911
Damn it!

357
00:21:52,914 --> 00:21:55,951
I've got it! I win!

358
00:21:59,421 --> 00:22:00,956
We're tied now.

359
00:22:01,189 --> 00:22:04,125
You're playing dirty!

360
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:07,629
Now for the last card.

361
00:22:07,829 --> 00:22:09,798
I'm going to complete this comeback.

362
00:22:10,031 --> 00:22:10,799
"We hope..."

363
00:22:11,299 --> 00:22:12,834
Let him finish, you cheat!

364
00:22:13,068 --> 00:22:14,803
This time I'm going to win!

365
00:22:16,771 --> 00:22:19,241
What? It won't open!

366
00:22:20,909 --> 00:22:24,913
Poor, naive Ryotsu. I locked that study just in case.

367
00:22:25,113 --> 00:22:26,114
Curse you!

368
00:22:26,314 --> 00:22:28,817
And so, the one to get the last laugh is...

369
00:22:29,150 --> 00:22:29,951
Huh?

370
00:22:31,052 --> 00:22:32,854
The key's gone? That's strange...

371
00:22:33,088 --> 00:22:36,992
Which means you can't get inside either...

372
00:22:37,225 --> 00:22:38,126
All right!

373
00:22:38,760 --> 00:22:39,527
Sorry!

374
00:22:40,629 --> 00:22:42,530
They're both taking their time.

375
00:22:45,233 --> 00:22:47,335
He went outside.

376
00:22:48,870 --> 00:22:50,305
Hmm? Huh?

377
00:22:51,506 --> 00:22:53,174
It's definitely not here.

378
00:22:54,509 --> 00:22:55,844
What's that noise?

379
00:22:58,947 --> 00:23:00,181
From in here?

380
00:23:03,618 --> 00:23:05,820
What's going on?

381
00:23:09,691 --> 00:23:11,292
Ugh, damn this door!

382
00:23:17,365 --> 00:23:19,200
My study!

383
00:23:19,434 --> 00:23:21,870
You just missed it, Chief.

384
00:23:22,203 --> 00:23:23,371
I win!

385
00:23:23,571 --> 00:23:26,808
But you did pretty well for someone your age.

386
00:23:27,008 --> 00:23:29,377
Next year's New Year's party—

387
00:23:29,577 --> 00:23:32,981
Next year's New Year's party...?

388
00:23:33,915 --> 00:23:38,887
You are definitely, absolutely, 100% not invited!

389
00:23:48,563 --> 00:23:52,334
Guess it's the same story this year.

390
00:23:56,604 --> 00:24:02,043
"We hope you enjoy KochiKame this year and many years to come."

391
00:24:03,144 --> 00:24:08,983
LIKE FATHER, LIKE SON
